      "id": 1,
      "text": "Zebulon Pike named Elk River in 1805 after the elk herds he saw along the Upper Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elk_River%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Elk River sits at the confluence of the Mississippi and Elk Rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elkrivermn.gov/1319/Elk-River-Historical-Walking-Tour",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Elk River was home to the first national bank in Sherburne County in 1870, Houlton Bank, located in downtown Elk River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elkrivermn.gov/1319/Elk-River-Historical-Walking-Tour",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elkhi Stadium, also known as Handke Station, was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2004.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elkrivermn.gov/1319/Elk-River-Historical-Walking-Tour",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Grist mills and a starch factory, which took advantage of the potato fields to the west, were built.",
